    "title": "March Madness tips off today. How to watch men's play-in games",
    "text": "March 17, 2026, 8:54 a.m. ETMarch Madness, every basketball lover's favorite time of the year, is finally here.The madness begins with the men's bracket. The play-in games, also known as the First Four, will start on Tuesday, March 17, in Dayton, Ohio. These games will determine the final spots in the round of 64.Here's what you need to know for the kickoff of the men's tournament:When does the NCAA basketball tournament start?The Men's NCAA Tournament begins with the First Four on March 17-18. The first round then takes place March 19-20.When are the play-in games for March Madness?Men's tournamentTuesday, March 17:6:40 p.m. ET: No. 16 UMBC vs. No. 16 Howard9:15 p.m. ET: No. 11 Texas vs. No. 11 NC StateWednesday, March 18:6:40 p.m. ET: No. 16 Prairie Views vs. No. 16 Lehigh9:15 p.m. ET: No. 11 Miami (OH) vs. No. 11 SMUWhat time is the first March Madness gameTip-off for the first March Madness game in the men's Division I bracket will occur at 6:40 p.m. ET on Tuesday, March 17.What channel is March Madness on?The First Four games will air on truTV. You can also stream them on the March Madness Live app and SlingTV.Where is the First Four for men's March Madness?The First Four will take place on the campus of the University of Dayton at UD Arena in Dayton, Ohio.When is the first March Madness game for the women's tournament?The first women's game of the 2026 NCAA tournament is March 18, starting with the First Four. The first round tips off March 20.NCAA printable bracketClick for your 2026 NCAA Men's Tournament printable bracketClick for your 2026 NCAA Women's Tournament printable bracketWhen are brackets due for March Madness?Here are the deadlines for March Madness brackets to be submitted for both the Men's and Women's NCAA Tournaments:All times EasternMen's NCAA TournamentUSA TODAY: Thursday, March 19 at noonCBS: Thursday, March 19 at noonYahoo!: Thursday, March 19 at 12:15 p.m.ESPN: Thursday, March 19 at 12:15 p.m.NCAA: Thursday, March 19 at noonWomen's NCAA TournamentUSA TODAY: Friday, March 20 at 11:15 a.m.CBS: Friday, March 20 at 11:30 a.m. ETYahoo!: Friday, March 20 at 11:10 a.m. ETESPN: Friday, March 20 at 11:30 a.m. ETNCAA: Friday, March 20 at noonUSA TODAY Network reporter John Leuzzi contributed to this report.",
